Harden NanoSVG against hostile geometry.

- nsvg__flattenShapeStroke(): with a non-finite segment length (dx*dx
  overflowing to inf) or dash lengths that scale to zero, the dash split
  point never advances and the loop never ends; a tiny dash over a huge
  path is merely unbounded. Cap dash segments per rasterization.
- nsvg__pathArcTo(): non-finite arc parameters made ndivs = (int)NaN,
  which is undefined and saturates to INT_MAX on the PSP's FPU (2^31
  cubic segments). Degenerate such an arc to a line.

--- a/src/nanosvg.h
+++ b/src/nanosvg.h
@@ -2292,6 +2292,14 @@
 	vy = (-y1p - cyp) / ry;
 	a1 = nsvg__vecang(1.0f,0.0f, ux,uy);	// Initial angle
 	da = nsvg__vecang(ux,uy, vx,vy);		// Delta angle
+	if (!isfinite(a1) || !isfinite(da) || !isfinite(cx) || !isfinite(cy)) {
+		// Non-finite geometry cannot be subdivided; (int)NaN below is
+		// undefined and becomes INT_MAX segments on MIPS.
+		nsvg__lineTo(p, x2, y2);
+		*cpx = x2;
+		*cpy = y2;
+		return;
+	}
 
 //	if (vecrat(ux,uy,vx,vy) <= -1.0f) da = NSVG_PI;
